    "type": "mc",
    "prompt": "A triangle is drawn inside a regular hexagon as shown. The value of $x$, in degrees, is:",
    "image": "qimages/kangaroo/ca-2022-g0708/q06.webp",
    "choices": [
      {
        "key": "A",
        "text": "15"
      },
      {
        "key": "B",
        "text": "30"
      },
      {
        "key": "C",
        "text": "45"
      },
      {
        "key": "D",
        "text": "50"
      },
      {
        "key": "E",
        "text": "60"
      }
    ],
    "answer": "B",
    "acceptedAnswers": null,
    "answerUnit": null,
    "solutions": [
      {
        "title": "Right triangle",
        "body": "Let the hexagon have side 1. The vertical side of the triangle joins two vertices that are one vertex apart, so it is a short diagonal of length $\\sqrt3$, and it is perpendicular to the top side of the hexagon (the hexagon is symmetric about the horizontal line through its centre, so this diagonal is vertical while the top side is horizontal).\n\nSo the triangle has a right angle at the top-left vertex, with legs 1 (top side) and $\\sqrt3$ (short diagonal). The angle $x$ lies opposite the leg of length 1, so $\\tan x = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt3}$ and $x = 30°$.\n\n**Answer: (B) 30**"
      },
      {
        "title": "Angles in the hexagon",
        "body": "The third side of the triangle is a long diagonal through the centre; it bisects the 120° angle at the bottom-left vertex, making 60° with the bottom side. The vertical side of the triangle is perpendicular to the bottom side (90°). Hence $x = 90° - 60° = 30°$.\n\n**Answer: (B) 30**"
      }
    ],
    "topics": [
      "geometry"
    ],
    "difficulty": 1,
    "duplicateOf": null,
    "reviewNote": null
