    "prompt": "Three sisters, whose average age is 10, each have different ages. When they get together in pairs, the average ages of two such pairs are 11 and 12. What is the age of the eldest sister?",
    "image": null,
    "choices": [
      {
        "key": "A",
        "text": "10"
      },
      {
        "key": "B",
        "text": "11"
      },
      {
        "key": "C",
        "text": "12"
      },
      {
        "key": "D",
        "text": "14"
      },
      {
        "key": "E",
        "text": "16"
      }
    ],
    "answer": "E",
    "acceptedAnswers": null,
    "answerUnit": null,
    "solutions": [
      {
        "title": "Turn averages into sums",
        "body": "The three ages add up to 3 × 10 = 30. The two pairs add up to 22 and 24. The sister missing from the first pair is 30 − 22 = 8, and the one missing from the second pair is 30 − 24 = 6. The third sister is 30 − 8 − 6 = 16.\n\nCheck: 8 + 16 = 24 (average 12) and 6 + 16 = 22 (average 11). ✓\n\n**Answer: (E) 16**"
      }
    ],
