        "title": "Chase the angles",
        "body": "Let $\\angle BAC = a$.\n\n- $AD = DB$: $\\angle ABD = a$, so the exterior angle $\\angle BDC = 2a$.\n- $CE = CD$ (and $E$ lies on $BD$): $\\angle CED = \\angle CDE = 2a$.\n- $BE = EC$: $\\angle EBC = \\angle ECB$, and the exterior angle $\\angle CED = \\angle EBC + \\angle ECB$, so $\\angle EBC = a$.\n\nThen $\\angle ABC = \\angle ABD + \\angle DBC = a + a = 2a$, and $\\angle ACB = \\angle ABC = 2a$. The angle sum gives $a + 2a + 2a = 180°$, so $a = 36°$.\n\n**Answer: (E) 36**"
      },
      {
        "title": "Check the answer",
        "body": "With $\\angle A = 36°$: $\\angle B = \\angle C = 72°$; $\\angle ABD = 36°$, $\\angle DBC = 36°$, $\\angle BDC = 72°$, $\\angle CED = 72°$, $\\angle DCE = 36°$, $\\angle ECB = 36°$. All three small triangles are isosceles as required.\n\n**Answer: (E) 36**"
      }
