    "answer": "A",
    "acceptedAnswers": null,
    "answerUnit": null,
    "solutions": [
      {
        "title": "Use the 30-60-90 triangle",
        "body": "The fold sends $A$ to $C$, so $EA = EC$. Triangle $EBC$ has a right angle at $B$ and $\\angle ECB = 30°$, so the side opposite the 30° angle is half the hypotenuse: $EB = \\frac12 EC = \\frac12 EA$.\n\nSo $AB = AE + EB = 3\\,EB$, and\n$$[ABCD] = AB \\cdot BC = 3\\,EB\\cdot BC = 6 \\cdot \\tfrac12 EB\\cdot BC = 6 \\cdot 15 = 90.$$\n\n**Answer: (A) 90 cm²**"
      },
      {
        "title": "Compare triangles",
        "body": "Triangle $AEC$ has base $AE = 2\\,EB$ and the same height $BC$ as triangle $EBC$, so its area is 30. Triangle $ABC$ = $AEC$ + $EBC$ = 45, which is half the rectangle. Rectangle: 90 cm².\n\n**Answer: (A) 90 cm²**"
      }
    ],
